Third-party notices
====================

Terminal engine (module :terminal-core)
----------------------------------------
The files under `terminal-core/src/main/java/com/termux/terminal/` are vendored,
with minimal changes, from the Termux project:

    https://github.com/termux/termux-app

  Upstream module: terminal-emulator
  Upstream commit: 3df69d1da197dd9bd71a3bafd902dffd720576b4
  Upstream licence: GNU General Public License v3.0 only

See `terminal-core/VENDORING.md` for the exact file list and the edits made to
get the engine compiling without its original pty/JNI subprocess code, which
this app does not use (Shellwave connects to a remote shell over SSH instead
of driving a local pseudoterminal).

Terminal renderer (module :app)
----------------------------------------
`app/src/main/java/io/github/lordofpolls/shellwave/terminal/TerminalRenderer.kt` is a Kotlin
port of Termux's `TerminalRenderer.java`, GPL-derived from the same upstream project and commit
as above:

    https://github.com/termux/termux-app
    Upstream path:   terminal-view/src/main/java/com/termux/view/TerminalRenderer.java
    Upstream commit: 3df69d1da197dd9bd71a3bafd902dffd720576b4
    Upstream licence: GNU General Public License v3.0 only

See the header comment in that file for what was changed in the port.

Text selection (module :app)
----------------------------------------
`app/src/main/java/io/github/lordofpolls/shellwave/terminal/TerminalSelectionState.kt` and
`TerminalSelectionOverlay.kt` are a Compose port of the selection-controller design in Termux's
`terminal-view` module - the coordinate model, the handle-drag clamp/snap behaviour, and the use
of the platform floating `ActionMode` for the selection action menu (Copy/Select All/Paste/Share
here, vs. upstream's Copy/Paste/More) - GPL-derived from the same upstream project and commit as
above:

    https://github.com/termux/termux-app
    Upstream paths:  terminal-view/src/main/java/com/termux/view/textselection/TextSelectionCursorController.java
                     terminal-view/src/main/java/com/termux/view/textselection/TextSelectionHandleView.java
                     terminal-view/src/main/java/com/termux/view/TerminalView.java
    Upstream commit: 3df69d1da197dd9bd71a3bafd902dffd720576b4
    Upstream licence: GNU General Public License v3.0 only

Unlike the renderer port above, `terminal-view` itself was never vendored into this repository
(only `terminal-emulator` was - see `terminal-core/VENDORING.md`) - these two files are a port of
its design to Compose (a `Popup`-hosted handle in place of `TextSelectionHandleView`'s
`PopupWindow`, and `TextSelectionCursorController.setInitialTextSelectionPosition`'s single-row,
column-by-column word scan - not `TerminalBuffer.getWordAtLocation`'s cross-row text-joining,
which an earlier draft of this port built on and which turned out to mishandle wide (CJK)
characters; see `wordSelectionAt`'s doc comment in `TerminalSelection.kt` for how that was found
and why the shipped version scans the way `TextSelectionCursorController` actually does), not a
line-for-line translation. See the header comments in both files for what was kept, adapted, or
left out.

